WEBVTT

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:12.330
You okay out here?

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.130
Could go for someplace less chilly, to be honest.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.080
We're fine!

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.580
You look pretty cold, though!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.170
<b>Support Magic</b>

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.540
I've got to have something that can keep us warm...

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.170
<b>Insulation Barrier</b>

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.790
Insulation Barrier!

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.920
That looks mighty warm.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.630
Perfect. This should keep me in working order.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:41.170
<b>Ricaardo</b>

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.170
This magic stuff never ceases to impress.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.960
Well I'll be, we don't get many tamers out here.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.670
Sure are dressed light for this bitter cold.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.250
What's going on around here?

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.250
This chill set in out of nowhere 'bout 10 days back.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.460
It's claimed more than a few of our own.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.630
What brings you out this way?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.630
I heard the food out here was worth the trip.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.750
Maa ikkatte ukenagashite

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.920
Nochi no jinsei wa henka shinakute

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.080
Mou ikka wa joushuu no te de

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.420
Boku no nouryoku wa imada sakanai

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.330
Katou tomosezu makeru koto mo itowanai nara

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:50.080
Mukishitsu na shinjou wa naze toki o utsu

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.250
Bokura dare mo ga himetaru chikara o motta monster

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.960
Da toshite mezame saseru koto naku ikitekuno

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.250
Oshikonde futa shite

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.000
Mou shinsen na kokoro janai

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:12.790
Sore demo kaoiro hitotsu kaezu ni ikiru monster

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.290
Dare mo ga mujikaku no sokojikara o uchi ni shinobaseru

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.000
Tsugi wa kimi no ban da

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.880
Tachimukaeyo monster

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:42.920
You heard right.
You should visit the Tiger's Flame Pavilion.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.330
Not many people around, huh?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.040
Seems like this area never used to get this cold.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.460
Glad this place was easy to find.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.080
Hope you don't mind the intrusion.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.080
I'm sorry, we're closed for the day.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.710
All right, what time do you open tomorrow, then?

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.290
Unfortunately we won't be open tomorrow, either.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:22.290
We've been forced to use all our firewood
for heating and have none left to cook with.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.670
I see...

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.540
But everything about this place
is telling me the food is amazing!

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.710
I'm not gonna let anything stop me from trying it!

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.710
So you just need some firewood?

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.380
Yes, but cutting down more trees now won't help.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:46.460
Freshly chopped wood produces too much smoke
to be used for cooking.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.580
It needs to sit and dry for a year, first...

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.630
Got it. Thanks.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.500
You okay there, Yuji?

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.330
We headed off again already?

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.580
Wait, weren't we s'possed to eat first?

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.040
Which of these trees is best for firewood?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.290
Who knows?

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.250
Beats me!

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.710
Couldn't tell ya!

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.080
Can't even offer ya a guess.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.750
Guess we might as well just cut a bunch down.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.880
What magic will do the trick...?

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.830
<b>Summoning Magic</b>

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.830
<b>Sage Skills</b>

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.000
Summon Axe!

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.540
Something about this feels wrong...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.000
But so be it.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:35.880
Never know...

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.880
<b>Super Combat Arts</b>

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.880
<b>Summon Axe</b>

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.710
...until you try!

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.790
I don't know if that was the axe
or the combat arts doing the work.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.830
This magic and all these skills really come in handy.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.130
Look at all this!

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.500
Like a work of art!

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.130
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.130
<b>Sage Skills  </b>

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.130
<b>Summoning Magic</b>

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.080
Now I need to dry it out.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.630
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.630
<b>Slime Moisture Absorb</b>

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.670
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.670
<b>Sage Skills  </b>

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.670
<b>Summoning Magic</b>

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.630
Can you guys use "Slime Moisture Absorb"?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.210
Ab-what?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.460
Never heard of it!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.630
Might it involve drinking?

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.170
Does it taste good?

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.170
<b>Tamer Skills</b>

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.170
<b>Slime Moisture Absorb</b>

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.880
Guess it's worth a shot.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.460
Slime Moisture Absorb!

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.790
That's yummy!

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.540
Yuji, this firewood's looking pretty dry already!

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.420
It's a lot lighter, that's for sure.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.540
Pack all this up for me, then.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.080
Can you guys fit all this?

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.130
'Course we can!

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.830
It's so light and perfectly dried!

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.670
Where did you find this?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.330
Can you use that to cook?

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.330
I'll go call the chef!

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.290
It's too dry.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.880
Fully dehydrated wood burns too strong.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.000
Can't cook anything good with wood like that.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.040
Slime Moisturization.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:15.000
I don't know how you made this firewood, but-

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:15.920
Will this work?

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.710
I'm telling you, this is no good...

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.000
What in the world is this?!

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.710
This heft! This is a perfect piece of firewood!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.040
I've never seen a piece so perfectly dried in all my life!

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:35.880
It's as if it exists solely for use in the kitchen!

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.420
Get the stoves lit!

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.130
R-right on it, chef!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.880
A perfect flame.

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.170
Where did you get this?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.130
My slime here made it.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.750
I won't feign to understand, but with firewood like this,
I can fix up something real special.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.460
Something "special"?

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:56.920
How much wood do you have?

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.580
I have about this much at the moment.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.000
Use Slime Moisturization to make
all of this just like that last piece.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.000
You got it!

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.830
Coming right up!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.170
We got this!

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.580
I never imagined slimes could do all this.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.710
If you need more I can go out and-

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.830
All right, we need to get you fed.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.920
I'll whip up some of my finest work.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:41.500
Here you are.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.040
Whoa-ho-ho-ho!

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.330
Sorry for the wait.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.250
That's grilled Angus Cattle with Rishia herbs.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.630
Steak and veggies!

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:52.790
It smells fantastic.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.040
Th-this flavor!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.670
The deliciously grilled beef hits first,

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:05.170
but it's swiftly followed by the sweet-yet-tart sauce made
from fresh vegetables, mixed with juices from the steak,

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.750
all coming together in a more full
burst of flavor than I've ever tasted!

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.670
There's no doubt in my mind...

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.580
this is the greatest work of culinary art I have tasted
since I woke up in this world!

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.500
Thank you for that.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:20.920
It was incredible.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.670
I could eat this for days on end.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:28.960
Our best dish is actually a stew,
but it takes a while to fix up so I opted for that instead.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.290
Stew?

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.580
I'll have to come back for it again tomorrow.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:36.920
But we really shouldn't be using
all this firewood just to cook here...

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:40.380
The whole town is low on wood to heat their homes.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.170
All you need is more firewood then, right?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.040
Well, yes, but...

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.670
I'll be back again tomorrow.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.040
Not that I have any idea how much firewood they need...

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.540
All anyone's looking for is firewood.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.290
I'd like to take on this job.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:22.580
Thank you. Is this your first firewood cultivation request?

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:23.750
Yeah.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:27.750
The guild requires firewood
to be cut to standard size and shape.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:35.880
You should start by heading out the Eastern gate to see
our firewood leader, Wodca, for further instructions.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.080
An adventurer, hmm?

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.080
<b>Special Woodcutting Instructor</b>

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.080
We won't turn away another pair of working hands.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.500
Can never have too much wood.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.920
The town needs five tons a day,
but we can't keep up with demand at all.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.960
Seems the situation is pretty dire.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.750
None of us were ready for a frost like this.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:12.540
Some nearby villages that weren't hit by this
have offered help, but it's far from enough.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.290
Is the village of Messias helping?

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:24.130
Messias? That place has been deserted
for a good while now.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.210
What was all that, then?

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:30.540
So, you ever cut firewood before?

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.420
You could say that.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.750
Just once today, though.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:40.170
Show me what you can do, then. We'll work from there.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.580
You don't look all that strong, so try not to overdo it...

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.460
WHAAAAAAAAT?!

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.630
Next we split up these logs into sections
and cut them down the middle, right?

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.830
Y-yeah...

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:16.460
Does 40 centimeters sound good?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.210
Yeah...

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.710
With two cuts down the middle?

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:20.830
Yeah...

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.790
And four cuts for bigger logs?

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:24.880
Yeah...

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.790
All set. Will this do the job?

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:28.880
Yeah...

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.790
I've got more than a few questions, but with
firewood this perfect, what I don't have are complaints.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:38.040
Thanks. I'll have my slimes dry all this out, then.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.040
What...?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.380
This tastes so good!

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:46.580
Say bye to that moisture!

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:48.790
What are you...?

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.170
I'll go cut some more.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.380
R-right...

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.500
Excellent work, Wodca.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.250
You're back early today.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.330
All thanks to that fella.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:11.040
He took down hundreds of trees at a time
and split them right into firewood.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.210
Used his slimes to carry it all here, too.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:20.460
With slimes? I didn't know magic like that really existed.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.210
You've heard of it before, though?

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:26.210
Well, I think I heard about it
at one of the churches before.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:31.580
There was a legend of a mighty beast master
who used slimes to transport things.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.040
Legends, huh? Maybe Father Steyl might know more.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.380
Better ask next time I see him.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.750
My slimes still have more firewood stored away,

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:43.960
but I don't think it will all fit in here.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.080
There's still about three days worth left.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:47.920
Three days worth?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.830
Fifty kilograms worth, then?

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.710
Huh? I heard you use five tons a day.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.420
Three days worth for the whole town?!

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.880
That should do it, Yuji!

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.130
Just like you asked!

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.630
I've never seen so much...

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:12.250
Is there still more?

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:13.960
I'm not even sure.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:15.960
Slime, how much do we have left?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:18.000
Another batch about this big.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.920
That's still only three days worth, though...

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:24.960
You still have other firewood jobs, right?

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:30.040
We do, but this is a lot of strenuous work, right?
Are you sure you're up to it?

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:36.130
They're worried after just this? Guess this world
really does care about its people more than home.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:13.750
Here you go. Ricaardo's famed Angus cattle
and Rishia herb stew.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:20.040
And for your friends we have some raw cuts
and a heaping helping of Rishia herbs.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.960
Now that looks good!

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:29.630
It's all on the town. I hear you did us
all a big favor out there.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Let's see, here...

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.880
The slow-stewed beef crumbles apart in your mouth!

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.290
But the flavor stays around,

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:48.670
playing a perfect harmony with the rich taste
of the vegetables in a miraculous symphony!

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.330
The rich flavor goes beyond
anything I've ever experienced,

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.210
exploding in a big bang level of divine glory!

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.750
This is a dish fit for the gods!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.420
I've never been more happy!

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.080
A glorious feast!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.500
I never tasted anything so good!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.880
I'll take another!

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.790
Liked it, eh?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:12.880
I'm glad I got to fix it up again for a change, but...

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:14.170
But...?

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:17.040
That's still not my best work.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:17.830
It isn't?!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:22.670
Our Rishia herb field has been
plagued by monsters lately, you see.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:25.630
They eat up all the very best herbs.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:29.250
And this is the only place
where anyone grows those things.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:34.710
I could fix up something better
if we had better herbs, but...

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.460
What sort of monster is giving you trouble?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:49.330
Let's split into two teams, one to search
for monsters and another to defend the field.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:50.460
Okay!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.420
We'll hold down the field!

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.630
Show yourself, monster!

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.210
We'll go find 'em!

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.000
Leave this to us!

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.420
They're in for a beating!

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:04.380
We'll show 'em what for!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.460
They'll be crushed to a pulp!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.960
We're looking for a Greedy Boar.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:12.790
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:13.460
It's bound to be somewhere in those woods,
but there's no telling how alert it is.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:15.210
Don't let your guard down.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.040
Don't worry, we'll get 'em!

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:23.080
<b>Sense Share</b>

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.670
I'll go this way!

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:21.080
Then I'll head that way!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.460
We'll track them down posthaste!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.670
Got an eye on 'em!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.380
Over here!

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:31.380
Prepare to meet your fate!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.710
You're going down!

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.670
Time to do this!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:39.710
We're in over our heads!

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.000
This ain't looking good!

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:42.830
Yuji! Send us some magic, quick!

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:43.830
Sheesh...

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:45.960
Fireball!

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:52.880
How's that for ya?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:54.170
Behold our strength!

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.460
And don't you forget it!

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:56.420
Heh-heh!

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.880
Your days of hoggin' all the Rishia herbs are over!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.750
There's more!

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.460
Over here as well!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.380
Let's take 'em both out in one go!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.500
We must have taken out at least 50 by now.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.710
The rest are getting harder to find.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:14.710
Yuji, we found something weird out here.

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.920
Something round and unusual.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.670
You don't know what this is, either?

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.250
No, I've never seen anything like it.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.580
But I sense faint traces of magic emanating from it.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:35.210
Oooh!

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:36.920
It took on a darker hue!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:37.960
Is it...?

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.540
Absorbing your magic, yeah.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.210
Must be a Dragon's Grace.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:42.880
What?

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.710
Wouldn't be surprised if this
is what gets turned into cursed magic stones.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.330
You might be right.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:58.000
That explains it! The magic in this area is weak
because this stone is absorbing it all!

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.830
Absorbing all the magic, huh...?

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:07.380
Can low levels of magic make it cold like this?

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:12.750
Sure can. Places with too much magic
get hot like volcanoes, too.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.790
So this frost is because of this stone, then.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:20.670
Do these things ever just appear naturally?

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:23.830
No, someone made this.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.880
There are traces of human magic that isn't yours.

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.920
Let me try and purify it.

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.170
We can look for whoever is behind this later.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:36.380
Anti-Magic Barrier!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.250
Dispel Curse - Extreme!

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.210
Wow!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:50.630
Slimes, spread out and see if you can find
any more of these stones.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.170
Roger!

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:03.250
Thoughtography!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.460
That's a total of 108 purified magic stone ores.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.630
All spread out in a perfect circle.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.580
Something's telling me we'll find something at the center.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:18.170
Which means...

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.540
...around here.

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.580
Slimes, you haven't picked up on anything?

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:42.170
Uhhh...

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:43.540
Seems like a normal forest.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.880
Nothing beyond the usual, I'm afraid.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:50.830
They're right, it does look normal,
but something still feels off.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.380
And I don't mean the unnatural clash
of greenery and snow.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:20:00.290
It's like there are bigger trees
intentionally put here to throw off the balance.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:03.290
Is this all some high-level camouflage?

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:05.630
Yuji, what's wrong?

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.380
Pick up on something?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:09.210
Something's wrong with this forest.

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:12.210
Everyone fall back away from this area.

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.460
Proud Wolf, help me get the slimes out of here.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:17.460
You got it!

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:18.750
Okay!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:19.880
Aye-aye!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.540
Yuji, what are you planning?

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:25.040
To destroy this forest.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.080
But you probably didn't want to hear that.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:36.290
No, it's all right. The forest will grow back over time,

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:42.670
but if they use cursed magic stones, there's no telling
what might happen to the ecosystem here.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.250
Good. Here goes, then.

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.290
Let it burn! Hellfire of Demise!

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:15.130
What is it?

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.330
An entrance to somewhere.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:18.750
Want to find out where?

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.250
Not really?

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:22.040
Yuji sounds excited.

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:23.380
Is this all for that little town?

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:26.750
Yup. I only need one reason to save that place.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:28.210
Huh?

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:33.210
They've got good food.

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:40.880
